SENSITIVITY += ('\n\n**Short-hours support.** ' + SHORT_HOURS_LIMITATION)
SENSITIVITY += r'''

**RUM-A/B estimation-input band defect.** The benchmark audit found that RUM-A's estimation input encoded the S12-native full employment-hours width, 26.5 rather than the S11 width 29.5, shifting its log average-hours-density input by the alternative-invariant constant -0.050856. That constant cancels from the conditional sampled-set likelihood, so the RUM-A estimates, standard errors, maximized criterion and criterion comparison are unchanged. RUM-B does not read those density rows. The stale RUM-A metadata and absolute opportunity-mass levels, and the old criterion-B reporting-bin moments for both benchmarks, were nevertheless defective: the corrected benchmark MAEs are {{n:mae_ruma|.4f}} and {{n:mae_rumb|.4f}}. No audited downstream level use was found, but the search was not exhaustive; absolute level uses of those inputs therefore remain a limitation.

**Numerically blocked opportunity-prospect metric.** ''' + WEA_STATUS + '\n'

CONCLUSION = clean_w1(v6.CONCLUSION)
